Implemented and executed in the focused environments:

- RFC 9580 v6 fingerprint/salt parsing and negative vectors; complete-key identities.
- purpose-separated `MRML-GIT-HYBRID-V1` AND verification and bounded trust transitions.
- ML-DSA self-verification, runtime entropy wrappers, malformed-key rejection, and volatile clearing of reviewed secret-derived intermediates.
- exact conventional SSH/OpenPGP commit and annotated-tag signature verification before local branch/tag ref mutation, with failure preserving the old head and absent tag ref.
- bounded Git object/pack/index parsing, deterministic fixed- and dynamic-Huffman level-9 LZ77 DEFLATE profiles, fixed-window/depth OFS delta selection, file-backed quarantine validation, OFS/REF delta resolution, authenticated thin-base completion, arrival packs, disk reservation, journals, atomic ref generations, recovery classification, and authenticated audit receipts.
- deterministic verification of every introduced commit, including merge-side ancestry, concrete detached hybrid proofs, and protected activation that consumes opaque verified state.
- canonical monotonic pair-validity/retirement state, authenticated purpose-separated key revocations, and generation-bound verification summaries derived only from opaque verified commit proofs.
- canonical full-fingerprint legacy-v4 validity/retirement/revocation policy state; policy membership alone remains inert and cannot bypass graph classification.
- bounded checkpoint/cutover graph classification with a valid conventional-v4 signature bound to exact commit bytes, complete fingerprint, trusted signing time, repository, and generations; every non-checkpoint-ancestry commit still requires hybrid evidence.
- canonical bounded pack-set manifests and an `MRREFS02` transition that atomically binds the exact manifest digest while advancing repository and pack generations; hosted receive cumulatively persists the selected set and reauthenticates exact selected arrival objects for subsequent thin bases.
- sequential protected receive history traversal over prior selected arrivals; the focused test prepares a second commit whose parent exists only in the first activated arrival generation.
- a transport-neutral `ReceivePackCore` composing request parsing, reservation, quarantine, complete-history verification, authenticated durable activation, receipt persistence, and report-status-v2 with injected verification-only and receipt authorities.
- exact selected-arrival composition for repository queries and upload-pack, with installed but unselected arrivals remaining invisible; hosted-Linux immutable exact-key pack caching, generation-safe compaction activation, and non-destructive local `git gc`/`git repack` pack/index installation.
- durable generation/context-bound detached proof records on Linux and exact-generation fetch-cache lookup/population with six-writer immutable contention coverage.
- overlapping thin receives using an authenticated base available only through the selected arrival set, with exactly one next-generation activation and the losing candidate remaining invisible; real child-process kill/reopen classification at the post-ref-activation/pre-journal boundary.
- bounded annotated-tag pages/details and verified metadata descriptors for exact source-manifest, source-lock, and build-receipt blobs without assuming ambient host paths or unsigned filename authority.
- bounded protocol-v2 request parsing, `ls-refs`, fetch framing, receive command/report framing, and repository-view boundaries without an external Git server runtime.
- deterministic bounded hostile-input corpora for Git pack/index/object/transport/trust/journal/ref-state/name/path parsers, OpenPGP packet/armor parsing, and ML-DSA key/signature verification on Linux and the Wine-hosted Windows target.
- six simultaneous process-local Linux fetch-pack generations from one immutable object graph, all byte-identical to the independently generated expected pack.
- conservative pre-body disk admission at the exact 2 GiB incoming-pack limit and fail-closed rejection at 2 GiB plus one byte, without allocating or consuming a body. This is boundary/admission evidence, not a completed 2 GiB stream or storage-performance run.

External evidence and deployment follow-ups (`REMAINS_OPEN`, non-blocking for core integration):

- The constrained compression, delta, exact-key cache, and reachability-compaction mechanisms remain inside the user-supplied `PATENT_REVIEW_PRELIMINARY_CLEAR_WITH_GUARDRAILS` screen recorded in `PATENT_SCREEN.md`. This is not a formal freedom-to-operate opinion; production sign-off by qualified Canadian patent counsel and shared review-log integration remain open.
- Deployment must provide the owner-controlled `ProtectedReceiveAuthority` implementation and key custody. The core now checks its exact policy authorization before consuming input, retrieves and verifies durable exact-context hybrid proofs, and uses the same authority boundary for authenticated receipts. Missing authority remains fail closed.
- The installed-as-`git` conventional profile remains distinct from a deployment-selected protected repository profile. Its public hybrid constructor self-verifies both components before changing a ref, but automatic policy/key-service selection belongs to deployment configuration and is not inferred from repository names or signature data.
- Exact-generation default-tip, every exact tag, and bounded caller-popular-ref precomputation is implemented without adaptive or similarity ranking. Real Linux processes prove the shared ref-activation serialization boundary; complete receive composition is additionally exercised process-locally. This is not a distributed load benchmark.
- Canonical threshold emergency recovery and durable one-use policy activation are implemented and tested on hosted Linux. Production recovery-key custody and approval generation stay outside the Git process.
- Constant-time timing evidence and independent cryptographic/security review remain open. The itemized 2026-07-31 FIPS 204 potential-updates mapping, checked-in mandatory NIST ACVP fixtures, and independent OpenSSL interoperability fixture pass on Linux and the Wine-hosted Windows target.
- Native Windows directory durability, process-kill fault injection at every other durable boundary, power-loss/physical-storage evidence, coverage-guided sanitizer/fuzz campaigns beyond the deterministic mutation corpus, multiprocess/distributed concurrency and peak-memory benchmarks, and production performance measurements remain open. Exact functional history-limit cases, process-local thread concurrency, and one hosted-Linux post-ref-activation/pre-journal child-kill boundary are covered, but do not satisfy those broader evidence requirements.
- Repository-specific release metadata discovery conventions, richer standard command forms, multi-round ACK negotiation, and integration with Agent B's listener remain partial. The supported protocol-v2 wants/haves profile and exact-generation cache are implemented; unsupported capability paths remain fail closed and are not advertised.
